# DURABLE REPRO for `todo/t1373` — `Box[T].get()` through a STRUCT-FIELD
# receiver is SILENT-WRONG ON THE DEFAULT BACKEND.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at pristine HEAD and unchanged by R50 Track A2):
#     C     → prints garbage (a pointer value, e.g. 187651060765344), rc 0
#     LLVM  → prints 9, rc 0
# `gg check` is clean, both builds are rc 0, and ASan reports nothing.
#
# MECHANISM, read off the emitted C rather than inferred — two call-emit shapes
# for the same operation, one of them deref-correct:
#     __v8  = &s.b;                                 /* the FIELD'S ADDRESS   */
#     __v10 = Box__Box__int64_t__get(__v8);         /* to a BY-VALUE __get   */
#     __v12 = Box__int64_t__get(*(Box__int64_t*)__v11);   /* sibling derefs  */
#
# ⚠ THIS INVERTS A FILED MEASUREMENT, AND THAT IS THE POINT. `todo/t0685`
# records `Box[int].get()` as green on both backends — TRUE FOR A LOCAL
# RECEIVER, FALSE FOR A FIELD ONE. The axis `t0685` enumerates is the PAYLOAD
# TYPE; the axis that actually discriminates is the RECEIVER PLACE. A fixture set
# sampling only local receivers is an anecdote on the axis that matters
# (Core #12). Do not merge this into `t0685` or `t0684` — a fix aimed at payload
# types leaves it alive.
#
# ⚠ WHY IT IS FILED HERE RATHER THAN ABSORBED BY R50 TRACK A2: A2 made
# `newtype NX(Box[int])` reach PARITY WITH THIS STRUCT CONTROL. The newtype and
# the struct now print the SAME garbage on C and the SAME 9 on LLVM, at every
# state of A2's patch including pristine HEAD. The control is what proves the
# residual wrongness is NOT A2's — it is this, one layer down in the C emitter.
#
# INTENDED (asserted by the `#[ignore]`d test): `9` on C and on LLVM.
# Un-ignore when the field-receiver call emit derefs like its sibling.
struct SB:
    Box[int] b

void main():
    Box[int] bb = Box(9)
    SB s = SB(^bb)
    print(s.b.get())
